---@class posthog.tasks.CreateTasksWarmRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field repository? string|distilled.Null Optional GitHub repository to clone, in `organization/repo` format (e.g. `posthog/posthog`).
---@field repositories? posthog.tasks.CreateTasksWarmRequestRepositoriesList GitHub repositories to clone into the warm sandbox, each in `organization/repo` format.
---@field github_integration? number|distilled.Null Primary key of the team's GitHub integration. Required when a repository is selected (it is what the sandbox clones with). Accepted without a repository too: the warm Run then boots with that integration's GitHub credentials, matching a repo-less create that carries it.
---@field branch? string|distilled.Null Branch to check out in the warm sandbox. Defaults to the repository's default branch when omitted.
---@field runtime_adapter? posthog.tasks.RuntimeAdapterEnum|string|distilled.Null Agent runtime adapter to warm the sandbox on ('claude' or 'codex'). The warm Run starts the agent on this runtime so a matching submit reuses it; a submit selecting a different runtime falls through to a cold Run instead of reusing a mismatched warm session. * `claude` - claude * `codex` - codex
---@field model? string|distilled.Null LLM model identifier to warm the sandbox on. A submit selecting a different model won't reuse this warm Run.
---@field reasoning_effort? posthog.tasks.ReasoningEffortEnum|string|distilled.Null Reasoning effort to warm the sandbox on for models that expose an effort control. * `low` - low * `medium` - medium * `high` - high * `xhigh` - xhigh * `max` - max * `ultracode` - ultracode
---@field sandbox_environment_id? string|distilled.Null Optional sandbox environment to provision before the task is submitted.
---@field custom_image_id? string|distilled.Null Optional custom base image to provision before the task is submitted; takes precedence over the environment's image.
---@field origin_product? posthog.tasks.WarmTaskRequestOriginProductEnum|string Product the warm Run is for. Fixed when the sandbox boots — it selects the OAuth app, the quota gate, the warm-pool budget, and PR authorship — so a submit only reuses a warm born under the same origin. Defaults to the Code app. * `user_created` - user_created * `posthog_ai` - posthog_ai * `signal_report` - signal_report
---@field initial_permission_mode? posthog.tasks.TaskRunBootstrapCreateRequestInitialPermissionModeEnum|string|distilled.Null Permission mode to boot the agent session on. Read at session construction, so it cannot be changed once the sandbox is warm — a submit selecting a different mode falls through to a cold Run. Omit to take the runtime's default. * `default` - default * `acceptEdits` - acceptEdits * `plan` - plan * `bypassPermissions` - bypassPermissions * `auto` - auto * `read-only` - read-only * `full-access` - full-access
---@field signal_report? string|distilled.Null Inbox report the warm discussion is about. Required with origin_product `signal_report`, where the warm Run boots repo-less and the submit that creates the report's discussion task activates it.

