---@class posthog.tasks.ListTasksRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field all_team_tasks? boolean Local development only. With ph_debug=true, list all project tasks for debugging. Ignored outside local development.
---@field archived? posthog.tasks.ListTasksRequestArchived|string Filter by archived state. Defaults to excluding archived tasks. Use 'true' to list only archived tasks, 'false' for the default, or 'all' to include both. * `true` - true * `false` - false * `all` - all
---@field basic? boolean With true, return basic list rows for summary surfaces: each row omits the full description and includes description_preview, its first 1000 characters. Defaults to false, which returns full task rows with description. The search parameter still matches description text server-side.
---@field channel? string Filter tasks to a channel's feed.
---@field ci_status? posthog.tasks.ListTasksRequestCiStatus|string Filter tasks by the CI check rollup on their most recent run's pull request, as last observed from GitHub. 'none' means the PR has no checks. * `passing` - passing * `failing` - failing * `pending` - pending * `none` - none
---@field client_provenance? posthog.tasks.ListTasksRequestClientProvenance|string Filter by the client that created the task * `posthog_desktop` - PostHog Desktop * `posthog_mobile` - PostHog Mobile * `posthog_web` - PostHog Web
---@field commented_by? number Filter to tasks carrying a thread comment written by this user ID.
---@field created_by? number Filter by creator user ID
---@field exclude_origin_product? posthog.tasks.ListTasksRequestExcludeOriginProduct|string Exclude tasks with this origin product from the results * `onboarding` - Onboarding * `account_audit` - Account audit * `error_tracking` - Error Tracking * `eval_clusters` - Eval Clusters * `user_created` - User Created * `slack` - Slack * `support_queue` - Support Queue * `session_summaries` - Session Summaries * `posthog_ai` - PostHog AI * `experiments` - Experiments * `signal_report` - Signal Report * `autoresearch` - Autoresearch * `signals_scout` - Signals Scout * `scout_suggestions` - Signals Scout Suggestions * `support_reply` - Support Reply * `hogdesk` - HogDesk * `review_hog` - ReviewHog * `image_builder` - Image Builder * `loop` - Loop * `mcp_analytics` - MCP Analytics * `signals_chat` - Signals Chat * `task_analysis` - Task Analysis * `workflow` - Workflow * `space_setup` - Space Setup * `business_knowledge` - Business Knowledge * `metrics_import` - Metrics Import * `knowledge_writer` - Knowledge Writer * `context_layer` - Context Layer * `feature_flags` - Feature Flags
---@field hog_flow_id? string Filter tasks to the runs spawned by this workflow's 'Create AI task' action.
---@field internal? posthog.tasks.ListTasksRequestInternal|string Filter by the internal flag, which controls whether a task is shown by default, not whether it is accessible. Defaults to excluding internal tasks. Use 'all' to include both internal and user-facing tasks, or 'true' to list only internal tasks. All values are available to any team member; access stays governed by task visibility. * `true` - true * `false` - false * `all` - all
---@field limit? number Number of results to return per page.
---@field mentions? number Filter to tasks whose thread mentions this user ID.
---@field offset? number The initial index from which to return the results.
---@field ordering? posthog.tasks.ListTasksRequestOrdering|string Sort order. '-last_activity_at' is newest activity first, where activity means a thread message or a run starting, streaming, or finishing. Defaults to '-created_at'. * `-created_at` - -created_at * `-last_activity_at` - -last_activity_at
---@field organization? string Filter by repository organization
---@field origin_product? string Filter by origin product
---@field pinned? boolean With true, only tasks the requesting user has pinned.
---@field pr_state? posthog.tasks.ListTasksRequestPrState|string Filter tasks by the state of their most recent run's pull request, as last observed from GitHub (webhooks plus the CI follow-up snapshot). * `open` - open * `draft` - draft * `merged` - merged * `closed` - closed
---@field repository? string Filter by repository name (can include org/repo format)
---@field search? string Case-insensitive substring search over task title and description. A numeric value also matches the task number. An empty value disables the filter.
---@field sources? posthog.tasks.ListTasksRequestSourcesList Only tasks from any of these sources. Repeat the parameter for each source, or send one comma-joined value or a JSON array. 'posthog_desktop', 'posthog_mobile' and 'posthog_web' match user-created tasks by the client that created them, and a user-created task from no other known client counts as desktop. 'posthog_web' also matches PostHog AI tasks. Any other value matches the task's origin product.
---@field stage? string Filter by task run stage
---@field status? posthog.tasks.ListTasksRequestStatus|string Filter tasks by the status of their most recent run. * `not_started` - not_started * `queued` - queued * `in_progress` - in_progress * `completed` - completed * `failed` - failed * `cancelled` - cancelled

